      "page_content": "1. Purpose\nThis policy defines approval authority levels for booking Order Intake and establishes requirements for Order Backlog\nmonitoring. This version supersedes v1.0 as part of the FY2025 controls enhancement program.\n2. Scope\nApplies to all Orders booked as Order Intake and to periodic review of Order Backlog balances.\n3. Approval Authority Matrix\nOrder Value | Approver\nUp to $100,000 | Sales Manager\n$100,001 – $500,000 | Regional Finance Head\nAbove $500,000 | CFO\nTHRESHOLD UPDATE\nApproval thresholds increased from $50,000 / $250,000 to $100,000 / $500,000. | \nApproval must be documented and retained in the order file.\n4. Order Backlog Management\n4.1 Review Frequency\nOrder Backlog is reviewed on a MONTHLY basis by the Finance team.\n4.2 Aging Calculation\nAging (Days) = Current Date - Original Order Booking Date\nAging (Months) = Aging (Days) ÷ 30 (approximate)\n4.3 Flagging Criteria\nBacklog items shall be flagged for review when EITHER:\n- Aging (Days) > 180 days (6 months), OR\n- No delivery milestone has been recorded in the system for 2 consecutive monthly review cycles\nFlagged items require Finance Manager review to determine whether continued recognition remains appropriate.\nCONTROL ENHANCEMENT\nReview frequency moved from quarterly to monthly; aging flag threshold reduced from 365 days to 180 days.\n5. Roles and Responsibilities\nRole | Responsibility\nSales Manager | Approves orders up to $100,000\nCFO POLICY FRAMEWORK | CONTROLLED DOCUMENT Page 2",
      "metadata": {
        "source": "C:\\Users\\USER\\Desktop\\RAG\\output_pdfs\\POL-ORD-003_v2.0_Order-Intake-Approval-Backlog-Management.pdf",
